<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξίτηλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξιέναι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>going out</i>: hence, <i>losing colour,
				fading, evanescent,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορφυρίδες ἐξίτηλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Oec.</u>
					10.3
				</span></i>
			; of paintings, <i>faded,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ὑπὸ τοῦ χρόνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					10.38.9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.44
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.150
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τροφή</span> food <i>that has
				lost its properties during assimilation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Alim.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; so of seed sown in alien soil, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				497b
			</span></i>; of a drug or wine <i>that has lost its power,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				10J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γενέσθαι,</span> of a family,
			to become <i>extinct,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.39
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔπω σφιν ἐ. αἷμα
			δαιμόνων</span> is not yet <i>extinct,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				162.4
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Criti.</u>
				121a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξιτήλου ἐόντος</span> where
				<i>attenuation</i> takes place, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Praec.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; of acts, <i>extinct, obsolete,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ χρόνῳ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					<u>Prooem.</u>
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				5.60
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				7.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.68b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Max.Tyr.
				16.2
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίχας ἐ. ποιεῖν</span>”
				<i>eradicate,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					2.76.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
